    <div class="help" id="help">
        <div class="cd-panel from-right">
            <div class="cd-panel-header">
                <a href="#" class="cd-panel-close">Close</a>
                <h2 id="helpTopic">Help topics</h2>
                <p class="cd-panel-print">
                    <a href="#" id="aPrint" onclick="printHelp(); return false;">Print</a>
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="cd-panel-container">
                <div class="cd-panel-content">
                    <div id="helpFile" class="showhide">
                                <input type="hidden" class="help-anchor" id="help-businessregistrationsdescription"/>
<h3>Business Registration Service</h3> 
<div><p>The Australian Government Business Registration Service combines a number of key government business and tax registration forms in one place.</p>
<p>We have forms for new businesses, existing businesses returning to apply for tax registrations or businesses who simply need <a href="https://digitalIDsystem.gov.au/" target="_blank">Digital ID</a>. See below for more details:</p>
<h4>New business</h4> 
<p>Use the <strong>New business</strong> form if you need a new Australian Business Number (ABN). You can apply here for your ABN together with any of the following registrations: </p>
<ul> <li>Business name*</li> <li>Goods and Services Tax (GST)</li> <li>Australian company</li> <li>Pay as You Go (PAYG) withholding</li> <li>Fringe Benefits Tax (FBT)</li> <li>Luxury Car Tax (LCT)</li> <li>Fuel Tax Credits (FTC)</li> <li>Wine Equalisation Tax (WET)</li></ul>
<p>*You can also <strong>apply for business name on its own</strong> if you: </p>
<ul><li>already have an ABN</li> <li>already have an ABN reference number</li> <li>apply as a joint venture.</li></ul>
<h4>Apply for tax registrations</h4>
<p>Use the <strong>Apply for tax registrations</strong> form if you already have an ABN, but need to apply for one or more tax registration.</p>
<p>You can use your <a href="https://digitalIDsystem.gov.au/" target="_blank">Digital ID</a> to apply for GST, PAYG withholding, FBT, LCT, FTC and WET.</p>
<h4>Can I register Norfolk Island businesses here?</h4>
<p>Yes. Norfolk Island businesses can use the <strong>New business</strong> form to apply for the following business registrations:</p> 
<ul><li>ABN</li> <li>Business name</li> <li>Australian company</li> <li>PAYG withholding</li> <li>FBT</li> </ul>
<p>Norfolk Island businesses do not need to register for GST, LCT, FTC or WET.</p>
<h4>Can I update my details or apply for renewals here?</h4>
<p>Not at the moment. To update or renew your registrations you&#39;ll need to refer to the correspondence you receive confirming your registration. </p>
<p>If you can&#39;t find your correspondence, visit the following agency websites to:</p> 
<ul><li><a href="http://asic.gov.au/changes" target="_blank">update your company details or annual statements</a> on the ASIC website</li>
<li><a href="http://asic.gov.au/your-bn" target="_blank">update or renew your business name</a> on the ASIC website</li>
<li><a href="https://www.ato.gov.au/Business/Registration/Update-your-details/" target="_blank">update your tax details</a> for your ABN, GST, PAYG, TFN, FBT, LCT, FTC, WET registrations on the ATO website.</li></ul>
<h4>Can I apply here for state licences or permits?</h4>
<p>No. You&#39;ll still need to find and apply for your business licences and permits on the <a href="https://ablis.business.gov.au/" target="_blank">Australian Business Licence &amp; Information Service (ABLIS)</a> website.</p>  <h4>Where do I go for help?</h4>
<p>If you have a question about the form or how your registrations are progressing, <a href="../../footer/footer/contactus" target="_blank">contact us</a>.</p>
</div>                                <input type="hidden" class="help-anchor" id="help-newabnregistrationtileheader"/>
<h3>Register your business</h3><div>
<p>Use this form if you need a new Australian Business Number (ABN). You can apply here for your ABN together with any of the following registrations:</p>
<ul>
<li>Business name*</li>
<li>Goods and Services Tax (GST)</li>
<li>Australian company</li>
<li>Pay as You Go (PAYG) withholding</li>
<li>Fringe Benefits Tax (FBT)</li>
<li>Luxury Car Tax (LCT)</li>
<li>Fuel Tax Credits (FTC)</li>
<li>Wine Equalisation Tax (WET)</li>
</ul>

<p>*You can also apply for business name on its own if you:</p>
<ul>
<li>already have an ABN</li>
<li>already have an ABN reference number</li>
<li>apply as a joint venture.</li>
</ul>

<p>You can register these types of companies here:</p>
<ul>
<li>Proprietary limited companies (also known as private companies) - the most common company structure used by small businesses</li>
<li>Public companies limited by shares or guarantee</li>
<li>Public companies with no liability</li>
<li>Special purpose companies (not for profit, home unit/body corporate, superannuation trustee)</li>
</ul>
<p>To register a private or public company that&#39;s unlimited (where the liability of shareholders is unlimited), you need to apply:</p>
<ul>
<li>by contacting the <a href="https://asic.gov.au/about-asic/contact-us/"target="blank">Australian Securities &amp; Investments Commission (ASIC)</a>, or</li>
<li>through a business service provider.</li>
</ul>
</div>                                <input type="hidden" class="help-anchor" id="help-existingapplicationtileheader"/>
<h3>Resume or track your application</h3>
<div> <p>You can resume unfinished applications, track the status of applications and search for specific applications through your application summary.</p> 
<p>To access your application summary, you need to select the type of application form you have started or submitted:</p> 
<p><strong>New business application</strong></p> 
<p>If you&#39;ve started or submitted an application for a new business registration such as a new ABN or business name, resume your application or track its progress by clicking on the first option.</p> <strong>Additional taxes</strong> 
<p>If you already have an ABN and have started or submitted an application for additional taxes, continue your application or view its status by clicking on the second option.</p> </div>                                <input type="hidden" class="help-anchor" id="help-additionalregistrationtileheader"/>
<h3>Register for taxes</h3>
<div>
<p>Use this form if you already have an ABN, but need to apply for one or more tax registrations.</p>
<p>You can use your <a href="https://digitalIDsystem.gov.au/" target="_blank">Digital ID</a> (attached to your ABN) to apply for:</p>
<ul>
<li>Goods and Services Tax (GST)</li>
<li>Pay as You Go (PAYG) withholding</li>
<li>Fringe Benefits Tax (FBT)</li>
<li>Luxury Car Tax (LCT)</li>
<li>Fuel Tax Credits (FTC)</li>
<li>Wine Equalisation Tax (WET).</li>
</ul></div>
                                <input type="hidden" class="help-anchor" id="help-newbnregistrationtileheader"/>
<h3>Register a company</h3>
<div>
<p>Use this form if you need to register one of these company types:</p>
<ul>
<li>Proprietary limited company (also known as a private company) - the most common company structure used by small businesses</li>
<li>Public company limited by shares or guarantee</li>
<li>Public company with no liability</li>
<li>Special purpose company (not for profit, home unit/body corporate, superannuation trustee).</li>
</ul>
<p>To register a private or public company that&#39;s unlimited (where the liability of shareholders is unlimited), you need to apply:</p>
<ul>
<li>by contacting the <a href="https://asic.gov.au/about-asic/contact-us/" target="blank">Australian Securities &amp; Investments Commission (ASIC)</a>, or</li>
<li>through a business service provider.</li>
</ul>
</div>                    </div>
